The driver fixes campaign ID `development-provider-two-evaluated-admission-20260908-01`, fresh artifact root `.artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/provider-admission-20260908-01` in the architecture worktree, and fresh disjoint resource roots under the main repository `.artifacts/pit-v5-admission-20260908-01`. It requires both selected parents to be absent, creates them exclusively after authentication of actual06, and rejects link/reparse roots, overlap, unexpected parents, or prior content. The fresh mounted data directory receives only the two authenticated data files.

It authenticates actual06's fixed manifest graph and imports exactly the 14 inventory dependencies plus the parent provenance sidecar and eight original request/output blobs. Typed dependencies and panel specs use their native repository loaders/writers; raw data uses exclusive exact-byte writes followed by native raw authentication; parent blobs use `append_binary_state` only in `development-parent-originals`. No old manifest, scope, config, launch/start/admission state, role state, ledger/reservation, owner, lease, checkpoint, archive, record, critic, response, or result is imported.

It then uses the reviewed native calls in this order:

1. `capture_development_policy_v5` at immutable commit `0985d9bae74162ec1da8a7268bd54e47f21b0b85`, checking the four exact policy blob hashes.
